Archive folder view and disk images
===================================

Maguro opens 7z, tar, and ISO files as folders by extracting them into a
cache directory. The shape of that feature (extract, then browse a real
folder) follows `browse_archives` in rustyfiles, which is MIT licensed:
https://github.com/gelenmedya/rustyfiles
The readers in this tree are Maguro's. No rustyfiles source is copied.

Crates added for this feature
-----------------------------

sevenz-rust2 0.27.0 — Apache-2.0
https://github.com/hasenbanck/sevenz-rust2
LZMA, LZMA2, and BCJ are part of the crate. This build also enables deflate,
bzip2, PPMd, and AES-256.

tar 0.4.46 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
https://github.com/alexcrichton/tar-rs

flate2 1.1.11 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
https://github.com/rust-lang/flate2-rs
Built with the rust_backend feature (miniz_oxide). No C zlib.

lzma-rust2 0.26.0 — Apache-2.0
https://github.com/hasenbanck/lzma-rust2
Used to read .tar.xz. Pure Rust.

bzip2 0.6.1 — MIT OR Apache-2.0
https://github.com/trifectatechfoundation/bzip2-rs
The default backend is libbz2-rs-sys (MIT OR Apache-2.0), a pure-Rust bzip2.
The C bzip2-sys feature is not enabled.

ppmd-rust 1.5.2 (via sevenz-rust2) — CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0
https://github.com/hasenbanck/ppmd-rust
zlib-rs (via sevenz-rust2's deflate feature) — Zlib license

The ISO 9660 / Joliet reader is written for Maguro and follows ECMA-119.
It does not use a third-party ISO crate.
